# TypeScript & Naming

- Use camelCase for all identifiers: properties, variables, functions, and IPC channel names.
- Drizzle schema objects use camelCase property names; the underlying SQL columns are snake_case (Drizzle maps them automatically).

## Shared types

- Shared types live in `packages/shared/src/types/` and MUST be re-exported from `packages/shared/src/index.ts`.
- Database row types (`SettingsRow`, `Vehicle`, `Record`, etc.) are defined as interfaces in the shared package. Prefer these over Drizzle inferred types; use inferred types only when necessary and always export them for consumers.

## No `any`

Avoid `any` unless absolutely necessary. Use proper generics or `unknown`.

```ts
// BAD
function handle(data: any) {}

// GOOD
function handle<T>(data: T) {}
function parse(data: unknown) {}
```
